%% Physics-based DRM indexing - wrought Ti-6Al-4V, alpha lath as a BOX ------
%
% THE WHOLE MODEL IN ONE PARAGRAPH ----------------------------------------
% An alpha lath is a box with three orthogonal face-pairs - (0001) basal,
% {10-10} broad face, {11-20} end face.  Etching rounds its 12 EDGES, and a
% rounded edge is a convex cylindrical mirror: it fans the light out along the
% great circle perpendicular to its axis, i.e. a STRIPE in the DRP.  Flat
% faces are ignored.  Partial etching is a single cut plane: only the top
% `etchFrac` of the rotated box height stands proud, and an edge contributes
% in proportion to the fraction of its length above that cut.
%
% That one rule produces the section-2.3.2 mechanism instead of asserting it:
%   Phi high (Fig 2.12 pt 1, 87.9 deg) - c lies in the surface, the box stands
%     on edge, the exposed edges are the four PARALLEL to c -> the dominant
%     stripe is PERPENDICULAR to c.
%   Phi low  (Fig 2.12 pt 4, 37.8 deg) - the basal face is near-horizontal and
%     forms the top, so its rim (perpendicular to c) is exposed -> the
%     dominant stripe is PARALLEL to c.
%
% WHERE THE CODE LIVES ----------------------------------------------------
%   cubeGeometryTi64            model setup: the triad, the 12 edges, 9 knobs
%   cubeReflectors              THE PHYSICS: rotate, cut, expose - MTEX-free
%   DRPsim_cube                 paints the exposed edges into a DRP
%   checkCubeMechanism          verification: decompose + overlay + print
%   makeDRPdic_cube             (Phi, phi2) dictionary at 5 deg
%   matchDRPcube                correlation match + azimuth shift search
%   check_indexing_result_cube  measured vs predicted at clicked pixels
%
% Read cubeReflectors.m top to bottom to audit the mechanism: every
% intermediate (tilt, exposed fraction, stripe azimuth, bevel maximum) is
% returned and printed rather than buried in an amplitude.
% -------------------------------------------------------------------------
addpath(genpath(fileparts(mfilename('fullpath'))));

addpaths = false;
if addpaths
    addpath("C:\Users\mrbla\Desktop\mrbla-downloads\Relevant Downloads\MTEX Code\mtex-6.1.0")
    startup_mtex
end

%% experiment (illumination) parameters ------------------------------------
% Section 2.3.2: 3 deg in phi, 5 deg in theta, theta in [10,65] -> 1440 images
exp_para.th_min = 10;
exp_para.th_max = 65;
exp_para.th_num = 12;
exp_para.ph_min = 0;
exp_para.ph_max = 357;
exp_para.ph_num = 120;

pos1       = [0 0 0 0];      % ROI; [0 0 0 0] -> draw one interactively
scaleCoeff = 0.5;
drmFolder  = "C:\\Users\\mrbla\\Desktop\\Cambridge\\Iven\\cropped_left";             % <<< PLUG IN YOUR Ti64 IMAGE FOLDER HERE >>>
                             % "" makes drp_loader open a folder chooser

%% crystallography ---------------------------------------------------------
% One crystalSymmetry drives the box triad, the dictionary and the IPF key.
exp_para.crystal = crystalSymmetry('6/mmm',[2.95 2.95 4.68], ...
    'X||a*','Y||b','mineral','Ti-alpha');

%% build the cube-lath model ----------------------------------------------
% Nine knobs, and only two of them really matter:
%   etchFrac  how deep the etch has gone, as a fraction of the rotated box
%             height.  THIS decides which stripe wins.  1 exposes all 12 edges
%             (symmetric asterisk); small values expose only the top family.
%   dims      [Lc Lb Lp] side lengths along [c, broad-face normal, end-face
%             normal].  Only ratios matter, and they double as the
%             edge-length weights.
% The rest shape the stripe: stripeWidth (cross-stripe half-width),
% bevelSpan/bevelSoft (how much of the great circle a rounded edge lights),
% stripeTaper (microfacet foreshortening), exposeExp (sharpness of the etch
% selection), edgeAmp (per-family reflectivity), combine.
%
% WHY dims IS NOT [1 1 1] ------------------------------------------------
% A LITERAL cube cannot be indexed.  With all three sides equal and all three
% edge amplitudes equal, a 90 deg rotation about any box axis maps the box
% exactly onto itself - and that rotation is not in 6/mmm, so two genuinely
% different crystal orientations give an IDENTICAL DRP.  Measured on a 5 deg
% dictionary: every entry has a twin at correlation 1.000, and the median
% round-trip misorientation is 90 deg, i.e. the map would be noise.
%
% A real alpha lath is a plate, not a cube: thin across its broad face, long
% along the growth direction.  Giving the three axes distinct lengths breaks
% the extra symmetry and the median round-trip error drops to ~2.4 deg, below
% the 5 deg grid step.  cubeAmbiguity below measures this for whatever you
% choose - run it before trusting a map.
%   dims = [1 1 1] is still one edit away if you want to see the cube case.
%
% The values below were chosen to satisfy BOTH requirements at once: they
% reproduce the Fig 2.12 dominance for all four points with a ~2:1 margin
% (see the check below) and they leave the dictionary essentially unique
% (ambiguity p90 = 1 deg).  edgeAmp indexes the three edge FAMILIES by the
% axis they run along - (1) broad^end, i.e. the prism^prism ridge parallel to
% c, (2) basal^end and (3) basal^broad, i.e. the basal rim - so [1 1.5 1.5]
% says the slow-etching basal plane leaves the crisper bevel.
exp_para = cubeGeometryTi64(exp_para, ...
    dims        = [1 0.3 1.5], ...   % [along c, across the broad face, along the end normal]
    etchFrac    = 0.30, ...
    exposeExp   = 2, ...
    edgeAmp     = [1 1.5 1.5], ...   % basal-rim edges survive etching best
    stripeWidth = 3, ...
    bevelSpan   = 0, ...
    bevelSoft   = 30, ...
    stripeTaper = 2, ...
    combine     = "sum", ...
    selfCheck   = true);

%% sanity check the mechanism with NO data --------------------------------
euPaper = [211.4 87.9  4.8;    % Fig 2.12 point 1
           160.3 87.7  4.2;    % Fig 2.12 point 2
           180.0 72.4  3.9;    % Fig 2.12 point 3
           289.2 37.8 28.0];   % Fig 2.12 point 4
checkCubeMechanism(euPaper, exp_para, ...
    labels = ["Fig2.12 pt1";"Fig2.12 pt2";"Fig2.12 pt3";"Fig2.12 pt4"]);

% Watch the stripe pair swap dominance as Phi sweeps:
%   checkCubeMechanism([0 20 0; 0 40 0; 0 60 0; 0 80 0], exp_para, verbose=false);
% Watch the etch depth do it, at fixed orientation.  NOTE cubeGeometryTi64
% rebuilds .cube from its OPTIONS, so any option you do not repeat reverts to
% its default - always carry dims and edgeAmp through, or you will silently
% re-create the degenerate cube.
%   for f = [0.05 0.3 0.6 1.0]
%       ep = cubeGeometryTi64(exp_para, dims=[1 0.3 1.5], edgeAmp=[1 1.5 1.5], ...
%           exposeExp=2, stripeWidth=3, combine="sum", etchFrac=f, selfCheck=false);
%       checkCubeMechanism(euPaper(4,:), ep, verbose=false);
%   end

%% can this model be indexed at all?  (still no data needed) --------------
% Simulates every dictionary entry against every other over every azimuth
% shift, and reports how far away a pattern's nearest indistinguishable twin
% is, plus a simulate-then-match round trip.  Run it whenever you change dims
% or edgeAmp - it is the difference between a map and a picture of noise.
%
% With the settings above expect roughly:
%   ambiguity radius  median 0.0, p90 1.0
%   round trip        median 2.7 deg (below the 5 deg grid step), with 20-30%
%                     of orientations beyond 10 deg
% That residual tail is intrinsic: a DRP of two stripes through the centre
% does not pin down every orientation, the same caveat the older lath model
% carries ("phi1 modulo 180, phi2 only weakly encoded").  Use res.score to
% mask it - the ambiguous pixels are not the low-score ones, so also check a
% few by hand with check_indexing_result_cube.
%
% With dims = [1 1 1] and edgeAmp = [1 1 1] instead, the median round trip is
% 90 deg: the literal cube is unindexable, and cubeGeometryTi64 warns.
amb = cubeAmbiguity(exp_para, resolution=5, nTest=60);

%% load sample dataset ----------------------------------------------------
[igray_sample, phitheta, pos, img_sample] = drp_loader( ...
    exp_para, pos1, format='jpg', scale=scaleCoeff, folder=drmFolder);

% convert into a DRP stack: [n1 x n2] cells, each th_num x ph_num
drp_original = igray2drp(igray_sample, phitheta, exp_para);

%% verify against MEASURED DRPs at points 1 and 4 ------------------------
% Pick the pixels whose EBSD orientation you know and read their DRPs out of
% drp_original.  NOTE the DRP viewer reports (col,row) while drp_original is
% indexed {row,col}.
%
% <<< PLUG IN THE PIXELS FOR THE Fig 2.12 POINTS HERE >>>
% m1 = drp_original{1099, 665}; % used a different drp path than the
% current one
% m2 = drp_original{1090, 619};
% m3 = drp_original{1038, 584};
% m4 = drp_original{1097, 568};
% checkCubeMechanism(euPaper, exp_para, measured = {m1;m2;m3;m4});
%
% The DRM azimuth zero and the EBSD sample X are mounted at a fixed rotation
% about the sample normal.  Sweep phiOffset until ONE value aligns the
% predicted stripes for ALL four points - that value is the registration.  It
% does not affect indexing, only this check.
% for off = 0:15:165
%     checkCubeMechanism(euPaper, exp_para, measured={m1;m2;m3;m4}, ...
%         phiOffset=off, verbose=false);
% end
%
% Then fit the two knobs that matter against the same points:
%   for f = 0.1:0.1:0.6
%       ep = cubeGeometryTi64(exp_para, etchFrac=f, selfCheck=false);
%       checkCubeMechanism(euPaper, ep, measured={m1;m2;m3;m4}, ...
%           phiOffset=<yours>, verbose=false);
%   end

%% dictionary + indexing --------------------------------------------------
% phi1 is not sampled: it is a rigid azimuthal rotation of the DRP, and
% matchDRPcube searches all 120 shifts by FFT.  phi2 runs to 180, not 60,
% because the BOX is 222 even though the crystal is 6/mmm.
[drpDic, euDic] = makeDRPdic_cube(exp_para, resolution=5);
res = matchDRPcube(drp_original, drpDic, euDic, exp_para);

%% results ---------------------------------------------------------------
index_num    = cellfun(@(x) sum(x,'all'), drp_original);
non_index_bg = index_num > 3e4;                    % tune this threshold
figure, imshow(non_index_bg); title('background mask (tune threshold)');

figure, imshow(plot_ipf_map(res.EUmap));
title('IPF-z, wrought Ti64 alpha (cube-lath mechanism)');

figure, imagesc(res.score); axis image; colorbar
title('match score (correlation; higher is better)');

%% validate: measured vs predicted DRP at clicked pixels -----------------
[drp_measurement, drp_predicted, xy] = check_indexing_result_cube( ...
    res.EUmap, drp_original, exp_para, score = res.score);
